{"born":[{"text":"9b21a06eb9","mother":2,"rewritten":false},{"text":"9b21a06eb9","mother":7,"rewritten":false},{"text":"b132719eae","mother":15,"rewritten":false},{"text":"8507b6853e","mother":11,"rewritten":true,"failure":null,"why":"The code distinguishes between definitively safe, definitely poisonous, and mixed-history fruits, adding cross-species risk assessment (similarity) to prevent eating new fruits that resemble known poisons, while prioritizing carrying only confirmed safe foods when hungry.","ms":10014},{"text":"9b21a06eb9","mother":20,"rewritten":false},{"text":"963d442fae","mother":15,"rewritten":true,"failure":null,"why":"The code improves safety by distinguishing between \"known poison\" (leave), \"known safe/full\" (leave if not hungry to conserve effort, otherwise taste/eat), and \"uncertain/unsafe history\" (eat only if critical, otherwise taste or leave). It uses recent history of non-harmed instances to cautiously approach unknown fruits via 'taste' rather than blindly 'eating' or 'leaving', balancing risk and reward for longevity.","ms":9327},{"text":"1d9526723d","mother":3,"rewritten":false},{"text":"9b21a06eb9","mother":2,"rewritten":false},{"text":"ffd60081fc","mother":7,"rewritten":true,"failure":null,"why":"The code prioritizes avoiding recently poisoned fruits to prevent repeated harm, prefers eating whole fruits that have consistently proven safe and effective at reducing hunger, and only tastes uncertain fruits when not starving, ensuring survival while maximizing energy intake.","ms":9578},{"text":"9b21a06eb9","mother":20,"rewritten":false},{"text":"1d9526723d","mother":3,"rewritten":false},{"text":"1d9526723d","mother":9,"rewritten":false},{"text":"1d9526723d","mother":4,"rewritten":false},{"text":"1d9526723d","mother":23,"rewritten":false},{"text":"1d9526723d","mother":4,"rewritten":false},{"text":"9b21a06eb9","mother":7,"rewritten":false},{"text":"89cb0b0c08","mother":23,"rewritten":true,"failure":null,"why":"The code prioritizes sa